1. Scope and definitions

This is a source-available copyright license. It applies to the original
software, research text, illustrations, documentation and other protected
material expressly distributed under this license (the "Material"). It
grants only rights the licensor owns or is authorized to grant. Separate
third-party notices and licenses take precedence for their material,
including the CC BY 4.0 experimental data and the embedded font software.
See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and the accompanying attribution inventory.

"Company" includes a commercial enterprise, sole proprietorship or other
entity when undertaking business activities. A Company's "Group" consists
of it and all entities that directly or indirectly control it, that it
controls, or that are under common control with it. "Control" means more
than 50% of voting interests or the power to direct management, by ownership,
contract or otherwise.

"Group Revenue" is the Group's aggregate worldwide gross revenue over the
12 months immediately preceding the use in question, eliminating internal
transactions to avoid double counting, measured consistently under its
ordinary applicable accounting standards. For a Group that has existed for
less than 12 months, use actual revenue since formation, without annualizing.
Include the relevant revenue of businesses acquired or reorganized into the
Group during that period; restructuring does not reset this test. Convert
non-US-dollar revenue using a documented, consistently applied published
central-bank or equivalent independent exchange rate for the period.
Revenue is not profit and is not limited to revenue attributable to this
project. The threshold is US$10,000,000; there is no employee-count test.

2. Permissions available to everyone

Subject to section 5, anyone may, without charge and regardless of revenue:

(a) read, inspect, download, retain, display and share unmodified public
copies of the Material, including public repository forks and archival
mirrors, for access, preservation, citation, education and scientific review;

(b) run, test and modify the released demonstrations to reproduce, check,
criticize or compare their published results, and publish the resulting
scientific review and the modifications necessary to reproduce that review;

(c) quote or reproduce attributed research text, figures and code excerpts
in scholarly articles, theses, teaching materials and scientific reviews,
and allow publishers and repositories to distribute those works, including
through publications that charge subscription or publication fees.

These permissions do not authorize incorporating the Material into a
Company's product, proprietary research system, paid service, customer
deliverable, commercial training corpus, marketing material or operational
workflow. Such use requires permission under section 3 or a separate license.
The exercise of rights already allowed by law is unaffected by this limit.

3. Additional no-charge permissions

For the following permitted purposes, the licensor grants a worldwide,
nonexclusive, no-charge license to use, reproduce, execute, modify, create
derivative works of, distribute, publicly display and perform the Material:

(a) Personal study, experimentation and noncommercial projects undertaken
in an individual capacity, rather than on behalf of a Company's business.

(b) Academic research and teaching undertaken by individuals, educational
institutions or nonprofit or public research institutions for scholarly
purposes. Receiving salary, public grants, tuition or ordinary publication
fees does not itself disqualify a use. Corporate sponsorship does not itself
disqualify independent scholarly research, but this exception does not cover
outsourced corporate development, proprietary customer analyses, commercial
product development or services performed for a Company's business. Calling
a project academic, placing it at a university or using an academic proxy
does not create an exemption for such Company use.

(c) A Company's business use while its Group Revenue is AT OR BELOW
US$10,000,000. This includes internal use and commercial distribution within
the limits of this license. A person or organization performing commissioned
development, integration or hosted execution on behalf of another Company's
business must also satisfy the revenue test for that Company's Group, or
obtain a separate license covering that use. An eligible intermediary does
not make an otherwise ineligible Company's use eligible.

Eligibility is assessed when the use occurs. If Group Revenue becomes
greater than US$10,000,000, further Company use outside section 2 requires
a separate written commercial license from the relevant rights holder.
Earlier eligible use remains authorized and does not create retroactive
fees. The user may stop the ineligible use instead of purchasing a license.
Retention of an inactive archival copy remains permitted under section 2.

